We are using Java JDK 1.3.1 on XP1000 machines. It works together with To=
mcat=20
4.1. I briefly tried kaffe but it wouldn't handle Tomcat=20
There is an rpm for the JDK here:
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/products/linuxdevtools/latest/jdk-1.3.1-1-linux-=
alpha.rpm=20

You will also need the following libs=20
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/products/linuxdevtools/latest/cpml_ev6-5.2.0-1.a=
lpha.rpm=20
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/products/linuxdevtools/latest/libots-2.2.7-2.alp=
ha.rpm=20

When converting the rpm with alien, a script necessary for cpml_ev6-5.2.0=
=20
installation is not translated: the following manual step takes care of t=
his=20

cd /usr/lib/compaq/cpml-5.2.0
rm -f /usr/lib/compaq/cpml-5.2.0/libcpml_ev6.so
ld -shared -o libcpml_ev6.so -soname libcpml.so    -whole-archive=20
libcpml_ev6.a -no-whole-archive -lots
strip libcpml_ev6.so
/sbin/ldconfig


But beware !: Because of a bug in glibc I have to use a libc version < 2.=
3.2-9=20
(2.2.5-11.5), see Bug#221969 (libc6.1 2.3.2.ds1-10 & 2.3.2-9 causes cause=
s=20
Segmentation fault in Java JDK1.3.1). That means I can only use the stabl=
e=20
"woody" version since I have not heard that this particular problem was=20
resolved

Hope this helps

Ulrich

